# Brain MRI Segmentation

A SegFormer-B2 model for FLAIR-abnormality masks on 2D LGG MRI slices. Native safetensors weights, an explicit foreground evaluation contract and original-source split identities are available in the [source repository]({{ github_url }}).

{{ artifact_contract }}

The result is a new replay with recorded model and data hashes. The historical checkpoint's training membership is unverified. The original hand-rolled U-Net checkpoint has not been recovered, so there is no corrected historical main-versus-baseline comparison. [Legacy reports]({{ github_url }}/blob/main/docs/BENCHMARKS.md) retain the old aggregates separately.

## Run the model

Use Transformers 5.5.4 or the project's locked environment, including torchvision.

```python
import numpy as np
import torch
from PIL import Image
from transformers import AutoImageProcessor, AutoModelForSemanticSegmentation

REPO = "{{ repo_id }}"
REVISION = "{{ artifact_revision }}"
processor = AutoImageProcessor.from_pretrained(
    REPO, revision=REVISION, backend="torchvision", trust_remote_code=False
)
model = AutoModelForSemanticSegmentation.from_pretrained(
    REPO, revision=REVISION, use_safetensors=True, trust_remote_code=False
).eval()
image = Image.open("slice.tif").convert("RGB")
# Float32 RGB [0,255] avoids uint8 rounding during tensor resizing.
inputs = processor(np.asarray(image, dtype=np.float32), return_tensors="pt")
with torch.inference_mode():
    logits = model(**inputs).logits
    logits = torch.nn.functional.interpolate(
        logits, size=(256, 256), mode="bilinear", align_corners=False
    )
    mask = logits.argmax(dim=1)[0]
```

The processor uses 256² inputs, rescaling 1/255, no ImageNet normalization and no label reduction. Actual predictions matched the repository path on eight committed TIF samples and one seeded nonsquare image: zero disagreeing mask pixels. [Numerical parity receipt]({{ github_url }}/blob/main/reports/provenance/processor-parity.json). This verifies computation paths rather than quality on unseen patients. The output mask corresponds to the resized input.

## Original data and protocol

[Mateusz Buda's LGG MRI dataset](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/mateuszbuda/lgg-mri-segmentation) contains 110 TCGA-LGG patients and 3929 image/mask pairs. The three stored image channels represent MRI sequences; missing sequences are substituted as documented by the dataset author. A slice's binary mask labels FLAIR abnormality.

The original source archive was retrieved and hashed. Running the sorted-patient/seed 42 preparation recipe recovers 3133/409/387 slices and 88/11/11 patients. [Source receipt]({{ github_url }}/blob/main/reports/provenance/lgg-source.json) · [Complete split manifest]({{ github_url }}/blob/main/reports/provenance/lgg-split-manifest.json) · [Evaluation contract]({{ github_url }}/blob/main/docs/EVALUATION.md).

Foreground Dice/IoU pool TP/FP/FN over all test pixels. Empty prediction and target score 1; false positives on an empty target score 0. The full report contains patient-macro measures, patient-cluster bootstrap intervals, per-slice/patient counts and prediction/target arrays. The limited cohort, 2D input and unresolved historical training lineage limit interpretation; clinical validation has not been performed.

